## 3. OfficeFloor POST-owners YAML and function classes

**Pipeline definition:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
Ordered chain: `require` (RequireOwnerFields) → `uniqueTelephone` → `uniqueHousehold` → `cityCapacity` → **`dailyLimit` (RequireDailyRegistrationLimit)** → **`build` (BuildOwner)** → `customerCode` (AssignCustomerCode) → `namesakes` (CountNamesakes) → `save` (SaveOwner) → `respond` (RespondWithOwnerCreated).

All function classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/` (BuildOwner, RequireDailyRegistrationLimit, AssignCustomerCode, MembershipNumber, CountNamesakes, SaveOwner, RespondWithOwnerCreated, etc.).

The response `membershipNumber` is produced by the mapper, not a pipeline step: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java:27-28` calls `MembershipNumber.of(owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate())`.

